From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:50:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] [Bugfix][Spec Decode] Propagate enable_cumem_allocator
 to the draft ModelConfig

The draft ModelConfig is rebuilt field by field from the target. Flags
outside that list read as defaults once the drafter builders re-inject
the draft copy into the parent VllmConfig via replace(), which re-runs
full VllmConfig validation. With a KV connector configured and
PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True, the KV-transfer
compatibility gate reads enable_cumem_allocator from the draft copy,
sees False, and aborts the worker even though the engine config
properly enabled the cumem allocator.

Copy the flag onto the draft config at construction, the same place
dtype and quantization already mirror from the target.
---
 vllm/config/speculative.py | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/config/speculative.py b/vllm/config/speculative.py
index d9c6b8a0b6..f847d01925 100644
--- a/vllm/config/speculative.py
+++ b/vllm/config/speculative.py
@@ -1389,6 +1389,17 @@ class SpeculativeConfig:
                     hf_overrides=draft_hf_overrides,
                     config_format=self.target_model_config.config_format,
                 )
+                # Memory-model flags must match the target: the draft config
+                # is re-injected into the parent VllmConfig (replace() in the
+                # drafter builders), which re-runs full validation. A flag
+                # set on the target but absent from this field list then
+                # looks disabled to any check that reads it from
+                # model_config, e.g. the KV-connector compatibility gate
+                # that exempts the cumem allocator from its
+                # expandable_segments rejection.
+                self.draft_model_config.enable_cumem_allocator = (
+                    self.target_model_config.enable_cumem_allocator
+                )
 
                 # Old-format Medusa checkpoints (e.g. FasterDecoding/medusa-*)
                 # omit vocab_size in config.json, so MedusaConfig falls back to
